  <h2>A safe daily workflow</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <strong>Confirm the active school year and semester.</strong> This prevents
      records from being added to the wrong academic period.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Check alerts and unfinished work.</strong> Resolve blocked
      enrollments, incomplete documents, payment issues, or full classes before
      starting new work.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Use the purpose-built action for the task.</strong> Avoid changing
      reporting statuses simply to move a record forward.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Read the confirmation message.</strong> KoAkademy explains whether
      an action was saved, queued, rejected, or needs another step.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Review the result.</strong> Confirm the student, academic period,
      amount, and next responsible office before leaving the page.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Configure enrollment without code</h2>
  <p>
    Enrollment Blueprints control who may enroll, required documents, subject
    and class assignment, tuition and payment rules, approvals, and
    notifications.
  </p>
  <p>Use this safe sequence whenever you configure enrollment:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Choose a preset and scope.</li>
    <li>Change only what is different for that school, student type, program, or period.</li>
    <li>Save the draft.</li>
    <li>Simulate a representative student and resolve every blocker.</li>
    <li>Publish the validated version.</li>
    <li>Activate the policy engine only when the readiness checklist is complete.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Publishing or activating a blueprint affects <strong>future enrollments
    only</strong>. Existing legacy enrollments remain legacy, and active policy
    enrollments keep the snapshot they started with. Continue with
    <a href="/docs/enrollment-policies/quick-start">Enrollment Blueprints → Quick
    start</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Before making an important change</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Confirm that you are working in the correct school and academic period.</li>
    <li>Read the "What this does" and impact guidance beside the setting.</li>
    <li>Test configuration changes with simulation before publication.</li>
    <li>Add clear change notes so another administrator can understand the decision later.</li>
    <li>Use rollback or reopen only through the authorized action provided by KoAkademy.</li>
  </ul>

